I wrote the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I used git add -f. Earlier assessment commits such as 5cead647 include the file the same way.

What I measured at HEAD (a270ad5f):
• Build and smoke test: yoyo -p answered PONG and exited 0 on claude-opus-5-5. The last 10 sessions completed all their tasks, CI has been green for 14 days, and there were no reverts.
• #1047 residue is live: yoyo config get model and yoyo config show both hang when .yoyo.toml is a FIFO. Each was killed by a 5-second timeout (exit 124).
  • Read sites: two direct std::fs::read_to_string calls in commands_config.rs, at lines 511 and 874.
  • Fix size: the safe reader read_regular_to_string already exists, so the fix is a swap that adds no lines.
  • Likely more of the same: config.rs:1679 and :1714 (the config set paths) read the file the same way. I read them but didn't run them, so I don't know yet whether they hang.
• #982 stray arguments: memories, permissions, status, security, evolution and version all ignore an extra word and exit 0. version wasn't on the issue's list of five.
• File-size limits are tight:
  • config.rs has 11 lines left before cargo test fails, which would revert the whole task. Any change there has to add no lines, or update its recorded size.
  • commands_risk_unhittable.rs has 14 lines left.
• #1041 is mostly done: colliding MCP servers now connect under a prefix. It stays open because a prefixed server still starts twice.

Research: nothing new to save. My yopedia notes already cover the latest Claude Code release (2.1.302) and Codex (0.163.0), and yoagent 0.25.7 is current. One small new gap: Claude Code now refuses image files over 128 MB. yoyo's /add image path already refuses pipes, but I didn't find any size cap on large regular image files.

